Z||000000||Fret Naught||01-14-2001||12:11 PM||||I spent some time yesterday, polishing my Alum. Wheels, and I got to thinking I wonder if there is some product on the market that makes this job easier. I have used mothers,<BR>never dull, & Hollywoods showshine. does anybody know of anything quick and easy?<BR>thanks<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FretNaught_sig_18.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||01-14-2001||12:14 PM||||I use Mothers mag and aluminum wheel polish. Wipe it on, wipe it off. It works great. It polished up a very dull set of exhaust trumpets perfectly. I love the stuff, and its easy to use.||||reg||1
Z||000002||overlord||01-14-2001||01:19 PM||||i used meguires gold class metal restorer, followed by Eagle 1 aluminum polish.<BR>works good....lot of buffing though||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||01-14-2001||10:07 PM||||Fret Naught - <P>Are you just trying to polish up rims that have been refinished before, or are you trying to get all the lathe marks, and any other sratches out?  If it is the latter, you have a lot of work to do, and the last thing to use is the Mothers, to "finish polish" it.  go to this thread to see the set I just got done with, and email me if you have any questions on the procedure that I took.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005246.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005246.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fret Naught||01-15-2001||02:05 AM||||Nope, I have a set of alum. wheels (American Racing) just trying to keep em looking good<BR>thought there might be a product out there that I was not aware of, seems you can keep on polishing and they just get brighter and brighter, lots of elbow greese. I am getting lazy in my old age I guess.<BR>Fret||||reg||1
